{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":26478,"ns":0,"title":"Real analysis","extract":"Real analysis is the part of mathematical analysis, especially as taught in undergraduate and graduate courses, that develops calculus rigorously over the real numbers and Euclidean spaces. Introductory real analysis is sometimes called advanced calculus, and studies limits, continuity, compactness, differentiation, integration, and series.","description":"Mathematics of real numbers and real functions","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}